--- body ---
## Context

The `status` verb was removed from %erg v1, but it keeps reappearing in
skill log examples (found in AGENTS.md, pick-ticket SKILL.md during the
2026-05-08 alignment raid). The class shape: any skill file containing a
log-line example can drift to use the old verb.

Individual fixes (0096, 0098) are not enough — without a standing gate, the
pattern will reappear in unrelated PRs. A CI grep catches it at the class level.

## Actions

In `scripts/skill-lint.sh` (or equivalent CI lint script), add a check:

```bash
# No legacy status verb in skill log examples
if grep -r '\bstatus open\b\|\bstatus closed\b\|\bstatus doing\b\|\bstatus pending\b' skills/; then
  echo "ERROR: legacy 'status <state>' verb found in skills/ — use 'note' or 'closed'" >&2
  exit 1
fi
```

Tune the pattern after reading the actual log-example contexts to avoid
false positives (e.g., `git status`, `http status`).

## Test

```bash
bash scripts/skill-lint.sh   # should pass on clean tree
# introduce a status verb in a skill and re-run — should fail
```

## Exit criteria

- `make check` or equivalent CI step runs the guard.
- The guard fails on a file containing `status closed` in a log example.
- The guard passes on the current clean tree.
